/E (It was just 5 days back, when Jubert, Brugune, Ziegurb and Ikneus were playing Cidrala in a yellow amber viscous lake, just at the side of a fairy- forest. At that time, the four boys were swimming, on the viscous lake, fighting each other using hands, legs, paws, claws, spells and the occult magic they had discovered on the lake, to knock each other out of the game, either by drowning a boy into deep depths, or by pushing a player out of the lake, or forcing him to float on air for 10 seconds. )
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [1 2]
>>
endobj
583 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 91 0 R
/E (Jubert still remembered the time. Ziegurb had held out a transparent glass can, from which several creatures - gruesome, horrifying and even macabre - were peering out of the can. Soon, they hissed and started approaching dangerously towards him. All of those snake heads hissing and mise-beast faces flexing their sharp teeth.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
584 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 91 0 R
/E (And when for the first time, a snake - of the thickness of a rope - jerked and tried to attack Ikneus, he jumped down and let the snake bite air. Soon, all of the snakes, tiny line baby wolves, Bingo-Reeches, spieres, flamers and baby muss-dragons kept attacking Ikneus, and he kept dodging every single attack with his occult, lithe movements. He was the prince-trainer of these movements, called Ludhaara arts. This form of physical art was highly esoteric on the planet, only people from a select few tribes and descendants get the right body type and the level of ebullience to learn this art form.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
585 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 91 0 R
/E (And Ikneus - a 13 years old boy - was training since he was four, and had only gulped the basics of this bellicose art form. Even he knew his training was going to become more demanding in the future.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
586 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 91 0 R
/E ("In future, I know I would have to keep a stiff upper lip and be ready to summon a lot of aplomb in demanding tasks," he had spoken to him once while taking a nap inside the in-tree cave with Ikneus.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
