/S /P
/P 93 0 R
/E (His elder sisters used to be his hostile enemies since when he was a kid. Brugune hadn't done anything yet his sisters threw him under the bus every single day, making sure for whatever mischief and blunders they did, Brugune could be blamed for everything; he would get scolded from his mommy and get beaten mercilessly by his daddy. Every day when no one was around, the sisters would beat him and bully him, leaving him with a torn heart to sleep with every night.)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
608 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 93 0 R
/E (This continued for years until one morning, when one of the sisters had nearly ended her brother's life. Danika gets shockwaves in her heart when she remembers the day even years after the tragic incident. The mere sight of seeing a gentle child, being thrown down from second floor, just to land on pieces of broken wooden chairs and furniture under the stairs. Blood slowly pouring out of his forehead... then his shoulders... then his back... it was raining on the floor. Soon, his entire body was painted with blood, while he remained still, unconscious on the pieces of broken furniture. No breathing, no pounding, no sign of life, just uncontrolled bleeding. Danika had shouted his name hundreds of times while trying to wake him up almost a thousand times, before she went to pieces.)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
